# Chase Content Graphics

**Canonical system:** [`Alphakiller1/chase-content-engine`](https://github.com/Alphakiller1/chase-content-engine)

**Bridge doc in this repo:** [`docs/CHASE_CONTENT_PLAN.md`](../../docs/CHASE_CONTENT_PLAN.md)

## Authority

| Concern | Where |
|---------|--------|
| Daily schedule, report contracts, PNG renderer, opinion overlays | `chase-content-engine` |
| Design law for social PNGs | `chase-content-engine/design/CONTENT_DESIGN_CONTRACT.md` |
| AI concept mockups only | `chase-content-engine/design/CHATGPT_IMAGE_MOCKUP_PROMPT.md` |
| Slate / offense / trajectory CSVs | this repo (`mlbma-pipeline/data`) |
| Dashboard UI tokens | `design/MLBMA_CURSOR_DESIGN_CONTRACT.md` (this repo) |

## Rules

1. Do **not** invent a parallel template catalog (T1–T5, etc.) in mlbma-pipeline.
2. Final graphics = `chase_content/render.py` + live bundle + approved logo files. Not Midjourney/ChatGPT image finals.
3. Image models may produce **concept mockups** with logo placeholders only — never drawn Chase/MLB marks, never publish those as posts.
4. Fix renderer conflicts listed in the content-engine design contract §14; do not weaken the contract.
5. `outputs/push_instagram.py` may publish captions/URLs; it must not invent layout. Image URLs should be engine-built PNGs.
6. Opinions are human editorial overlays (`MY BET` / `LEAN` / `WATCH` / `PASS` / `NO OPINION`) — never auto-inherited from model projections.

## When asked to “make a graphic” here

Point at the content engine, outline migrate → validate → build → human QA, and only change this repo if the **data contract** (CSV fields / freshness) needs work.
